It's not right to say NetHack doesn't have a GUI. It clearly does; it's
just ASCII-based rather than pixel-based. The problems with the latter
can be fully appreciated by looking at this screenshot:

http://www.lionhead.com/bw/screenshots/10a.jpg

That's Black & White, from only 5 years ago. Those graphics were
state-of-the-art. Any attempt at a "pretty" GUI will look laughably
dated in short order. See NetHack's tiles interface, for example.
That's fine for a commercial game that nobody plays 5 years later, but
for a game with long-term appeal like NetHack, the novelty soon wears
off, the eye candy soon turns sour, and the graphics begin to detract
from the actual gameplay. And in terms of popularity, well... the tty
interface is timeless /and/ retro-cool.

